[{:db/id "41376f0b-fddb-515b-9135-0dcfd4896483" :answer/id #uuid "41376f0b-fddb-515b-9135-0dcfd4896483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}} + 12 t^{3} (3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "809bb840-826d-5090-ab24-5ba97394b73e" :answer/id #uuid "809bb840-826d-5090-ab24-5ba97394b73e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6df73b83-3780-5113-98c9-ae7f6c812078" :answer/id #uuid "6df73b83-3780-5113-98c9-ae7f6c812078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12 t^{3} (3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :answer/id #uuid "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e92b5772-4089-5199-9617-602bbe124f77" :answer/id #uuid "e92b5772-4089-5199-9617-602bbe124f77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1a990c52-96e6-5a56-8e2a-37b3d1997675" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a990c52-96e6-5a56-8e2a-37b3d1997675" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["41376f0b-fddb-515b-9135-0dcfd4896483" "809bb840-826d-5090-ab24-5ba97394b73e" "6df73b83-3780-5113-98c9-ae7f6c812078" "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" "e92b5772-4089-5199-9617-602bbe124f77"] :answer-field/correct "811d9993-cbf5-58f2-82af-df6589b0f550" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "379f3d57-a4e8-5653-a290-2e107a7dab3c" :question/id #uuid "379f3d57-a4e8-5653-a290-2e107a7dab3c" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=3 t^{4}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =9 t^{8} e^{3 t^{7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=12 t^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(3 t^{7} e^{3 t^{7}} + e^{3 t^{7}})\\cdot (12 t^{3})+(9 t^{8} e^{3 t^{7}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =12 t^{3} e^{3 t^{7}} + (36 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}) + (27 t^{10} e^{3 t^{7}}) \\\\  & =3 t^{3} (21 t^{7} + 4) e^{3 t^{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["1a990c52-96e6-5a56-8e2a-37b3d1997675"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "212f23b1-5655-5afe-ac3f-c0a1b51cbabf" :answer/id #uuid "212f23b1-5655-5afe-ac3f-c0a1b51cbabf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}} + 3 t^{2} (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1849c99c-ec5f-564e-bd00-2693ebbb1567" :answer/id #uuid "1849c99c-ec5f-564e-bd00-2693ebbb1567" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :answer/id #uuid "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9928a079-eba2-5e28-93d4-777658d1302b" :answer/id #uuid "9928a079-eba2-5e28-93d4-777658d1302b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3 t^{2} (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4b78b10d-4899-5250-a89d-b0ffe4794c07" :answer/id #uuid "4b78b10d-4899-5250-a89d-b0ffe4794c07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "03c9cabd-fbbb-5023-88c9-3c2c7ba49282" :answer-field/id #uuid "03c9cabd-fbbb-5023-88c9-3c2c7ba49282" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["212f23b1-5655-5afe-ac3f-c0a1b51cbabf" "1849c99c-ec5f-564e-bd00-2693ebbb1567" "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" "9928a079-eba2-5e28-93d4-777658d1302b" "4b78b10d-4899-5250-a89d-b0ffe4794c07"] :answer-field/correct "77c6e33f-6d12-5c5d-b983-ae5efd0acca4" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4946f9ea-a5fa-50ee-8aec-931b80816d77" :question/id #uuid "4946f9ea-a5fa-50ee-8aec-931b80816d77" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=t^{3}$ and $y=t^{2},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =t^{6} e^{t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=3 t^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=2 t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2})+(t^{6} e^{t^{5}})\\cdot (2 t) \\\\  & =3 t^{2} e^{t^{5}} + (3 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}) + (2 t^{7} e^{t^{5}}) \\\\  & =t^{2} (5 t^{5} + 3) e^{t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["03c9cabd-fbbb-5023-88c9-3c2c7ba49282"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "0753e31c-5005-5a9b-a87b-f91a8c8a77a7" :answer/id #uuid "0753e31c-5005-5a9b-a87b-f91a8c8a77a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 t (2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :answer/id #uuid "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "60fde45f-357e-58f4-affa-c5ef9a2b31ce" :answer/id #uuid "60fde45f-357e-58f4-affa-c5ef9a2b31ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}} + 4 t (2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "447c7f99-fdb6-5457-8d9a-e3aa9f50861f" :answer/id #uuid "447c7f99-fdb6-5457-8d9a-e3aa9f50861f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d5960284-1fb4-5fe6-a6cc-93c721a5098b" :answer/id #uuid "d5960284-1fb4-5fe6-a6cc-93c721a5098b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e3d976a4-de41-5ed3-b5d4-88d3dc494011" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d976a4-de41-5ed3-b5d4-88d3dc494011" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["0753e31c-5005-5a9b-a87b-f91a8c8a77a7" "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" "60fde45f-357e-58f4-affa-c5ef9a2b31ce" "447c7f99-fdb6-5457-8d9a-e3aa9f50861f" "d5960284-1fb4-5fe6-a6cc-93c721a5098b"] :answer-field/correct "e8702b54-5e62-56c8-9256-f605b63609ca" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "77e86c5a-4b57-5eb8-8644-abcaf34b69bc" :question/id #uuid "77e86c5a-4b57-5eb8-8644-abcaf34b69bc" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=2 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{3},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =4 t^{4} e^{2 t^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=4 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3 t^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(2 t^{5} e^{2 t^{5}} + e^{2 t^{5}})\\cdot (4 t)+(4 t^{4} e^{2 t^{5}})\\cdot (3 t^{2}) \\\\  & =4 t e^{2 t^{5}} + (8 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}) + (12 t^{6} e^{2 t^{5}}) \\\\  & =4 t (5 t^{5} + 1) e^{2 t^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["e3d976a4-de41-5ed3-b5d4-88d3dc494011"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "1e1c7a8e-0422-5233-b088-e2341346c984" :answer/id #uuid "1e1c7a8e-0422-5233-b088-e2341346c984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "5b61d18a-70d2-5b67-a497-85ceecaad618" :answer/id #uuid "5b61d18a-70d2-5b67-a497-85ceecaad618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8 t (4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6f1b3dcf-deeb-5278-88c3-40be3d31308c" :answer/id #uuid "6f1b3dcf-deeb-5278-88c3-40be3d31308c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :answer/id #uuid "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e024a943-4b21-5e6c-99ff-b264cf508bf5" :answer/id #uuid "e024a943-4b21-5e6c-99ff-b264cf508bf5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- 64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}} + 8 t (4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b48d05a5-03ed-527d-b03e-d22708b9e3bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "b48d05a5-03ed-527d-b03e-d22708b9e3bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["1e1c7a8e-0422-5233-b088-e2341346c984" "5b61d18a-70d2-5b67-a497-85ceecaad618" "6f1b3dcf-deeb-5278-88c3-40be3d31308c" "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" "e024a943-4b21-5e6c-99ff-b264cf508bf5"] :answer-field/correct "774a3c97-56bd-5fbe-bf9f-4aa50c321d1d" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "ba6447ed-c55a-5176-ab21-a18af111a0e0" :question/id #uuid "ba6447ed-c55a-5176-ab21-a18af111a0e0" :question/problem "If $f(x,y)=x e^{x y},$ $x=4 t^{2}$ and $y=t^{4},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}$." :question/worked-solution "![](images/f0/f01b253f560405a8c0f4be8f8797c652fb0ddf774f4db110b8822313b8ac50f3.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y)$ with one independent variable $t,$ where $x=x(t)$ and $y=y(t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} &=x y e^{x y} + e^{x y},\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x^{2} e^{x y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $t,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} &=8 t,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=4 t^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =(4 t^{6} e^{4 t^{6}} + e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (8 t)+(16 t^{4} e^{4 t^{6}})\\cdot (4 t^{3}) \\\\  & =8 t e^{4 t^{6}} + (32 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) + (64 t^{7} e^{4 t^{6}}) \\\\  & =8 t (12 t^{6} + 1) e^{4 t^{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["b48d05a5-03ed-527d-b03e-d22708b9e3bd"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "e85d9162-b4d4-547e-bd9a-0d23fbc8ff6f" :answer/id #uuid "e85d9162-b4d4-547e-bd9a-0d23fbc8ff6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2 t (t^{5} e^{t^{5}} + e^{t^{5}})" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6c364802-b683-5589-9cbc-78d6e2193cf5" :answer/id #uuid "6c364802-b683-5589-9cbc-78d6e2193cf5" :answer/type :answer.ty